Carrier balance: DEP 632 mg; DPG 1000 mg; TEC 480 mg; IPM 20 mg; ethanol 60 mg. Total carriers 2192 mg. Ambrox Super's 480 mg dose contributes exactly 120 mg product + 280 mg DPG + 20 mg IPM + 60 mg ethanol from its recorded 3/7/0.5/1.5 g preparation. No displacement volumes are asserted.

Every row's ODT/OAV authority is provisional repository screening only. The associated JSON preserves exact arithmetic and NULL authoritative volumes; the pipeline report retains its own threshold values. Orris Liquid, Tonkarome and Suederal product ppm must not be converted into pure-irone, pure-coumarin or single-molecule ppm.

## 7. Material selection rationale and survival criteria

All choices below are hypotheses to test, not claims that more materials improved the perfume.

| Material | Loss on omission | Strongest alternative considered | Dominance / survival criterion |
|---|---|---|---|
| Hedione | Less space between powder and warm interior | Hedione HC | Reject if floral air displaces iris; HC adds an unnecessary grade change |
| Ambrox Super | Less dry amber continuity | Ambrofix crystals | Existing exact mixed stock avoids a new crystal preparation; reject abrasive amber takeover |
| Iso E Super | Less woody separation and contour | More Bacdanol | Sandalwood adds body, not the same space; reject generic woody aura |
| Benzyl Salicylate | Less cosmetic cushioning | Benzyl Benzoate | BB is a carrier/control candidate, not the same floral function; omit if only heaviness remains |
| Patchouli EO | Loss of an advertised dark anchor | Clearwood | Cleaner reconstruction changes natural shadow; reject muddy/camphoraceous dominance |
| Bacdanol | Loss of sandalwood body | Ebanol | Ebanol is a different stronger sandalwood candidate; do not stack by default |
| Kephalis | Iris-to-amber transition may disconnect | Vertofix Coeur | Drier cedar shifts the seam; reject tobacco-led character |
| Cashmeran | Less textile grain | More Iso E Super | More space does not replace grain; omit if it merely thickens woods |
| Suederal | Loss of optional suede seam | Safraleine | Saffron/spice is unwanted; keep only if blind omission loses coherence without improving identity |
| Ambrettolide | Less close floral/musk rounding | Habanolide | Cleaner/metallic veil is a different hypothesis; choose one after carrier-matched comparison |
| AIMI | Collapse of main iris body | Beta Ionone | More fruity violet is not the same body; refuse duplicate AIMI/Givaudan counting |
| Alpha Irone | Less specific irone accent | More AIMI | Broad body does not guarantee the accent; retain only with distinguishable benefit |
| Orris Liquid | Less dry root product texture | Orivone + Alpha Irone | Defined molecules are a possible alternative, not equivalent to this product; do not infer assay |
| Alpha Ionone | Less petal approach to iris | Beta Ionone | Beta's fruity direction risks violet takeover |
| Orivone | Less dry root edge | More Orris Liquid | Product increase changes multiple facets; reject woody/earthy spike |
| Tonkarome | Less rounded roasted-tonka interpretation | Tonka Absolute 10% | Natural stock basis/composition unresolved; this known mass stock does not prove pure coumarin |
| Coumarin | Less dry hay-tonka definition | More Tonkarome | Base composition unknown; retain only if it adds definition rather than redundant sweetness |
| Heliotropal | Less almond-powder link | Vanillin | Vanilla moves toward gourmand icing; omit if almond/confectionery is salient |

Do not remove a target character solely because a questionable ODT/VP model reports OAV below 1. Such a result is a data/role alarm requiring evidence. Conversely, do not retain a prestige ingredient merely because a role has been written for it.

## 8. Exact stock reconciliation and gaps

Worktree inventory materialization succeeds. Its overlay is not silently replaced by the canonical checkout's different schema/lineage.

- AIMI and the Givaudan AIMI label bind to one physical stock (canonical 2026-09-04 identity correction; V5 row 21). Exact trade-grade equivalence is not asserted.
- Alpha Irone is the owned 10% w/w DEP stock, not neat.
- Orris Liquid uses canonical INV-USER-20260905-001: 9% w/w supplied PerfumersWorld 8IQ24653 product in DEP. Worktree's unstated-carrier record is incomplete. Neither 9% pure irones nor GC-O identity is established.
- Ambrox Super is the 25% w/w mixed-carrier stock. Ambrofix liquid/crystals are distinct and unused.
- Ambrettolide 10% w/w DPG and Tonkarome 20% w/w TEC use exact canonical 2026-09-04 user records. The worktree runtime still has incomplete/missing bindings; its resulting holds are retained.
- Suederal neat is explicitly in the live inventory, while the runtime materializer exposes only the ambiguous 10% stock. The formula chooses the neat physical-list line, not that ambiguous dilution. This mismatch is a runtime-binding gap, not proof the neat bottle is absent.
- Coumarin powder and neat Heliotropal are owned; the two formula working stocks below are PLANNED, not falsely recorded as existing.
- No Guaiacwood, depleted musk, unsafe forced stock substitution, unspecified saturated Coumarin or duplicate Cashmeran stock is used.

Missing-chemical impact: no required external purchase. Missing evidence is more important than a missing molecule: Orris product identity/assay and physical stock densities constrain quantitative modeling; exact stock preparation and safety records constrain future execution. These are localized gaps. No product purchase, inventory pin change or shared data repair is authorized.

## 9. Preparation ledger — future work only

PLI-PREP-C20: 2.000 g owned neat Coumarin powder + 8.000 g DEP = 10.000 g, nominal 20.000% w/w supplied powder. Label material, preparation ID, date, masses, carrier, basis, preparer and observations. Do not use either existing basis-unspecified 20% DEP or approximate saturated DPG bottle. Proposed solution must become and remain homogeneous at the working/storage conditions; if it does not, HOLD this prepared-stock route and revise explicitly.

PLI-PREP-H10: 1.000 g owned neat Heliotropal (Piperonal) + 9.000 g DEP = 10.000 g, nominal 10.000% w/w. This is not Heliotropin Fleuressence. Same labeling/homogeneity requirements. Do not assert that this proposed concentration has already passed a solubility/stability test.

These are preparation specifications, not reports that anything was mixed. The smallest stock transfer in the 6 g master is 40 mg; use a balance whose verified uncertainty is at most 1% of the smallest intended transfer (0.4 mg here), or scale the entire master up. Never assume 0.001 g display readability proves that uncertainty. Piperonal's 10 mg product dose is transferred through 100 mg prepared solution. No sub-10-µL neat dosing instruction is issued.

No heat, solvent substitution, topping up, evaporation correction or use of a partially crystallized stock is authorized by this document. Such changes need a recorded preparation revision.

## 10. Future mixing and nominal 30 mL finish

Do not execute until the stock preparations, remaining quantities, handling requirements and appropriate safety review are resolved. Card is a future-work design artifact, not a release receipt.

1. Record exact bottle/lot and stock-preparation identity; verify clear/homogeneous condition and balance suitability. Protect volatile stocks from evaporation.
2. Weigh the basket-ordered stock additions in the separate card. Finish each basket before moving to the next; mix appropriately between additions without unrecorded solvent.
3. Verify 6.000 g master mass (or an exact common scale factor), homogeneity and no visible precipitation. Record actual masses and departures instead of silently correcting the last component.
4. Use enough proportional master to obtain a measured 6.00 mL aliquot at a recorded temperature. Weigh that aliquot and retain the record. A 12.000 g proportional master is an optional planning scale, not an instruction to waste surplus.
5. Transfer to calibrated final-volume equipment and bring to 30.00 mL with suitable perfumer's ethanol. Record actual final mass, ethanol used, clarity and temperature. 24.00 mL ethanol is only the naive additive estimate, not the final-volume instruction.
6. Observe development, haze/crystals and odor at predefined intervals. No skin trial is inferred from a clear solution.

## 11. Controlled experiment, not another formulation tree

Protect AIMI, Alpha Irone, Patchouli, Tonkarome, Coumarin, Bacdanol and Ambrox doses in the first comparison. These define the core target interpretation.

First test only Suederal (optional, unadvertised leather interpretation): A = complete formula; B = same masses of every other stock, with the 40 mg Suederal replaced by 40 mg DEP in the 6 g master. This holds total mass and every declared stock-carrier contribution constant except the necessary product-to-vehicle substitution. The replacement vehicle is explicitly recorded; active load is NOT held constant. Suederal's proprietary internal composition prevents a fully matched unknown internal carrier claim.

Next, only if needed, test texture detail as one declared module: remove Orivone 40 mg + Cashmeran 60 mg + Heliotropal working stock 100 mg. Replace with 90 mg DEP to preserve its known carrier plus 110 mg DEP as documented product-replacement vehicle. All other rows stay unchanged; total remains 6 g. This tests that combined module only, not each material separately.

Single-musk alternative: compare the 800 mg Ambrettolide stock (80 mg product + 720 mg DPG) against 80 mg neat Habanolide + 720 mg DPG. Same product mass and declared carrier mass, not equal odor intensity. Do not include both musks in the full design merely to avoid this decision.

Use blind codes assigned independently of evaluation order. Make at least two independent preparations of each comparison arm and balance A/B order across separate sessions. For controlled trials, dilute equal weighed master aliquots to the same recorded final mass with the same ethanol, instead of independently topping each arm to volume and calling the matrices matched. Record the specified product-replacement vehicle difference. Keep application mass, substrate, matrix preparation, elapsed times and room conditions the same. Evaluate on blotters only after handling/safety clearance, not by an automatic skin instruction. Schedule 0, 5, 30, 120 and 240 min, with a 24 h blotter observation only as exploratory. Obtain free descriptions before scoring separately: Intense-target recognition (iris + darker amber/patchouli + tonka/sandalwood), coherence, iris continuity, unwanted takeover and liking. Include an authentic reference only if actually available and record its identity.

Acceptance is qualitative and scoped: keep a module only if it contributes a repeatable target-linked distinction without worsening identity/coherence. No effect, contradictory sessions or fatigue means UNRESOLVED; do not invent a significance test or similarity percentage from two personal sessions. No physical tests have run.

## 12. Computational screen contract and current limitations

The executable pipeline accepts raw volumes, not this exact mass ledger. The associated DIAGNOSTIC_ONLY Markdown encodes mg as unit-density surrogate µL solely to exercise the existing pipeline. This is an artificial interface assumption, not a density measurement. Neither its stock-equivalent active µL nor its modeled ppm supersedes Section 6.

Run with an explicit Intense-specific family key. This key is not in the current registry; preserve the resulting unknown-family HOLD/FAIL rather than substituting original Prada or Dior. No immediate parent is supplied because this is an original proposal.

Known pre-run data issues: Bacdanol profile VP = 0.001 Pa versus IFF approximately 0.142 Pa at 23 C; Ambrettolide profile VP = 0.003 Pa versus IFF approximately 0.0211 Pa at 23 C. Temperatures and product provenance are not identical, but the discrepancies are too large to treat output as confirmed. Kephalis local 0.46 Pa and manufacturer's 0.53 Pa also differ. No shared physics data is edited.

Patchouli has an existing composite constituent model; its fixed fractions cover only a subset of the oil and are not a GC-O receipt for the owned lot. Orris Liquid also receives a repository natural-mixture decomposition, but the actual supplied product's extraction/assay/GC-O is unverified. Its modeled constituent claim is therefore not admitted as stock truth. Tonkarome/Suederal single-species surrogate ODT/MW likewise cannot establish mixture headspace.

Numeric gamma is an assumed model parameter; values of 1 in the registry are not evidence of ideal behavior. OAV is a screening ratio with medium/unit and threshold provenance requirements, not perceived share, universal detection, liking, safety or resemblance. Mixture interactions and assessor sensitivity remain unmeasured.

